  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The average time taken&nbsp;by a moving particle between successive collisions or impacts is referred to as the mean free time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#964;</mi></mfenced></math>.</p><p>The average distance a moving particle travels between successive collisions or impacts is referred to as the mean free path <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#955;</mi></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>So, the mean free time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
